// PlatformMlx, the Mlx port (PORT.md): JSCOnly's configuration (bmalloc,
// WTF and JavaScriptCore are JSCOnly's, built with config.JSC_ONLY: the
// lines that shape their headers, the event loop, the allocator, the C
// loop, are the same here) with what a port's Options<PORT>.cmake decides
// for WebCore and PAL: Skia on the CPU (no encoders, no OpenType SVG), the
// Adwaita theme and the page's dark appearance (DARK_MODE_CSS, as GTK and
// WPE: the desktop's scheme through Page::setUseColorAppearance),
// HarfBuzz shaping, WOFF through zlib, Unix domain sockets' handles for
// shared memory (as GTK and WPE); composited layers on the CPU (M8:
// coordinated graphics with TextureMapper's sources, as WPE has them, and
// their asynchronous scrolling on a scrolling thread, damage tracking,
// kinetic scrolling and wheel event regions as PlatformEnableGlib.h gives
// GTK and WPE; the port's MlxLayerTreeHost composites them with
// SkiaCompositingLayer, PORT.md "Compositing"), WebGL (1 and 2) on
// ANGLE's Vulkan backend (USE_ANGLE; GraphicsContextGLMlx.cpp, PORT.md
// "WebGL"), no media (video, web audio, GStreamer, WebRTC), no XSLT, no
// notifications, no accessibility bridge (ATSPI, ATK), no GLib's
// libraries (libsoup, GCrypt, xdgmime), no Little CMS, AVIF, JPEG XL or
// WOFF2. JSCOnly defines no PLATFORM(), so every choice is one of these.
// ENABLE_BINDING_INTEGRITY is off: its check compares an object's vtable
// pointer with `&_ZTV<class>[2]`, the Itanium ABI's address point, and
// mlx-cc's vtables have their own layout (the pointer is the symbol's
// address): every XMLHttpRequest, fetch Response and WebSocket failed it.
// (JSC_ONLY's has it off too, where nothing reads it.)
// USE_FONT_VARIANT_VIA_FEATURES is off, where GTK and WPE have it on: their
// text of more than a character with kerning or shaping goes to the
// complex (HarfBuzz) path through a PLATFORM(GTK) || PLATFORM(WPE) branch
// of FontCascade (shouldUseComplexTextControllerForSimpleText) a JSCOnly
// build does not have; with it off, FontCascade::codePath sends that text
// there itself, so it is kerned as GLib's layout tests expect. (Small caps
// are then synthesized when a font has no smcp, not asked of HarfBuzz.)
